<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Szeged</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1444">1444</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade-of-varna">Crusade of Varna</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szeged">Szeged</a> was a ten-year truce agreed in 1444 between the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>. It restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durad-brankovic">Đurađ Branković</a> to his Serbian Despotate and returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smederevo">Smederevo</a> to him. Within weeks the Hungarians broke it to launch the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> that ended in disaster at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a> in November 1444.</p></div>
